# Clean branch before commit

Before making commits, confirm you are on a non-`main` branch created from current `origin/main`.

## Before the first commit on new work

1. `git fetch origin main`
2. Create the branch from the updated tip: `git checkout origin/main -b <type>/<short-description>`

## Before pushing

```bash
git fetch origin main
git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD
```

Every commit listed should belong to this task. If you see unrelated commits, fix history before push.
